      "nets": ["Net-(U2-VCC)", "GND"],
      "observed": "U2 pin 28 (VCC, pintype power_in) is connected only to C3 pin 1 on the isolated net Net-(U2-VCC); C3 pin 2 is on GND. U2 pin 28 is not present on the main VCC net, even though other SSD1306 supply pins such as U2 pin 6 (VBAT) and U2 pin 9 (VDD) are connected to VCC.",
      "expected": "The SSD1306 VCC supply pin should be connected to the main VCC rail, with C3 serving as its bypass capacitor to GND. A power_in supply pin should not be left on an isolated net containing only a capacitor to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"22\") (name \"Net-(U2-VCC)\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"28\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(pin (num \"28\") (name \"VCC\") (type \"power_in\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C7 (2.2 µF) — U4 `VCC` (digital-logic supply pin) to GND"}
      ],
      "impact": "The OLED driver's VCC/analog supply node is not powered and is left floating, so the display may fail to initialize, remain dark, or behave unpredictably.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist otherwise matches the Portal specification's functional connectivity, but U2 pin 28 (SSD1306 VCC) is tied only to a bypass capacitor and not to the VCC rail, which is a likely missing supply connection."
}

